    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1013">

                <pb facs="0980" n="882" xml:id="pg882"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr.
                            Peirce.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-08-04"><hi rendition="#italic">August 4,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 170.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I confirm your telegram<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d1013-f1"/> of the 2d instant.</p>
                <p>Judge Embry, attorney in the case of the <hi rendition="#italic">C. H.
                    White</hi>, thinks that some of his evidence is wanting to the proof of his
                    case. He will write to you the particulars.</p>
                <p>Whenever the evidence is completed in all the cases, and has been presented in
                    such form as to make it admissible and competent for the consideration of the
                    arbitrator, you may sign the protocol.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
